diff --git a/docs/IOS18-JIT.md b/docs/IOS18-JIT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0f132fe
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/IOS18-JIT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+# Experimental iOS 18 JIT compatibility work
+
+Base: `ca3183ea3dfb0fd706aff1bea2abb871b5d27aec` (willfaust/Madeira v0.1.1).
+
+## Status
+
+Candidate patch, **not a validated iOS 18 port**. The host allocator tests pass.
+No macOS runner has been dispatched and no IPA has been produced at this stage.
+The local execution host is Linux, without Xcode. GitHub browser authentication
+is required to create a fork and dispatch the prepared workflow.
+
+## Crash investigation
+
+The reported iPhone 13 / iOS 18.5 failure is SIGTRAP, BRK immediate 61453
+(`0xf00d`), in `jit26_prepare_region` called from `StikJITHelper.allocatePool`.
+That function unconditionally issued Madeira's debugger RPC instruction.
+StikDebug's `ProcessInfo.hasTXM` returns false before iOS 26, and its HomeView
+only enters the script path when hasTXM is true. A normal legacy JIT enable
+therefore does not establish the BRK-serving script Madeira expects.
+`CS_DEBUGGED` persists after detach and cannot establish that the script is
+listening. This explains the reported breakpoint, but does not establish that
+Wine/FEX will otherwise work on this phone. The original full crash file was
+not available in this workspace; the reported stack and trap immediate were
+recovered from the preceding conversation.
+
+## Changes
+
+* Preserve the existing `jit26_prepare_region` symbol, dispatching pre-iOS-26
+  calls to a legacy Mach VM backend after checking `CS_DEBUGGED`.
+* Allocate writable/executable backing, transition the canonical view to RX,
+  verify effective and maximum permissions, then retain the existing shared
+  RW-alias creation and Wine/FEX placement constraints. No MAP_JIT entitlement
+  or blanket signal-handler workaround is introduced for iOS 18.
+* Reject zero, overflowing and unaligned requests. Release newly owned memory
+  and Mach object ports on failures. Do not free caller-owned existing regions.
+* Skip script URL data, BRK detach and trap-handler installation on iOS 18.
+  Skip Wine's optional page-zero BRK fallback on iOS 18 as well.
+* Stop the execution diagnostic if preparation fails. Clean up the RX allocation
+  if creating/protecting its RW alias fails in the Swift and FEX pool paths.
+
+The iOS-26-and-later backend is otherwise retained; this patch does not solve
+its script-readiness detection or non-TXM hardware selection. No app-wide iOS 18
+compatibility claim follows from this change.
+
+## Verification performed
+
+```
+cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror tests/host/jit-legacy-test.c -o /tmp/jit-test
+/tmp/jit-test
+git diff --check
+bash -n build/ci/build-unsigned-ipa.sh
+python3 build/ci/check-app-inputs.py
+```
+
+The C test executes the production legacy helper with mocked Mach operations.
+It covers allocation, page rounding, coalesced VM regions, invalid inputs,
+allocation/protection/query failure, silently missing execute permission,
+insufficient maximum protection, port cleanup and caller-owned mappings.
+It cannot validate the real iOS kernel's JIT policy, alias coherence, cache
+maintenance or execution. The input check correctly exits 2 for missing inputs.
+
+## Build blockers and prepared workflow
+
+`.github/workflows/ios18-jit.yml` runs on `macos-15`. Its default validation mode
+compiles the allocator against the iPhone SDK, parses the changed Swift files,
+runs the host test and uploads an input report. **It is not a complete native
+dependency bootstrap.** Swift parsing is not type-checking or an app build.
+
+The optional app-packaging stage uses Debug (as required by upstream), disables
+signing and produces a Payload ZIP only after xcodebuild succeeds. A fresh
+checkout cannot currently reach that stage: 15 referenced archives are absent,
+including the FEX libraries, Wine unix/server libraries, DXMT and FFmpeg.
+
+Upstream `docs/BUILDING.md` is the starting recipe, but inspection also found:
+
+* `build/wineserver/build.sh` requires an existing base `libwineserver.a`.
+* `build/dxmt-ios/build.sh` refreshes an existing combined archive; when absent,
+  it prints a note rather than creating the combined LLVM/DXMT library.
+* Wine scripts require generated `wine/build-macos` headers/configuration.
+* The LLVM iOS build and FreeType inputs also need provisioning.
+
+After GitHub access is available, first run SDK validation, fix any compilation
+errors, then complete the native bootstrap (or obtain matching reproducible
+build inputs). Merely enabling `build_app` on the current workflow will report
+missing dependencies; it cannot produce a usable emulator from this checkout.
+
+## Required device validation
+
+1. Sideload the successfully built IPA with development/get-task-allow signing.
+2. Start a fresh process with JIT disabled: allocation must fail without SIGTRAP.
+3. Enable ordinary StikDebug JIT on iOS 18.5, then allocate the pool. Confirm the
+   log selects `legacy Mach VM`, valid RX placement, and successful RW alias.
+4. Verify alias coherence and execute the existing JIT test (expected 42).
+5. Start Wine, then a small guest program; exercise session exit and relaunch.
+6. Check iOS 26 with the Madeira script for regression separately.
+
+Packaging and sideloading do not themselves enable JIT. Real-device failures
+after pool allocation may require further Wine/FEX, graphics or memory changes.
+
+## Rebased onto v0.1.1
+
+The October 2 release adds debugger-presence checks and a kernel-placement retry
+for the RW alias on 63 GB maps. Both are retained. On the legacy backend, JIT
+readiness accepts CS_DEBUGGED without a live debugger, the trap fallback stays
+disabled, and allocation failures use the new user-visible poolFailure field.
+The official release still requires iOS 26; it is not an iOS 18 compatibility fix.
+
+## Build bootstrap continuation
+
+Authenticated access revealed an existing successful build in shkoios/Madeira.
+Imported its native bootstrap scripts (source ref recorded in git history),
+adapted the DXMT path and FEX patch to v0.1.1, and disabled only the optional
+rusage profiler when compiling against an SDK older than 27. The hosted build
+uses a clean pinned v0.1.1 checkout plus the combined patch. This bootstrap is
+pending runner verification; the earlier missing-input report is historical.
